## Root cause

Two distinct bugs, both invisible to `tsc`:

1. **`await` on an `Output<T>`** — `pulumi.Output` is *thenable-ish* only inside `apply` callbacks; awaiting it at the top level detaches the value from the dependency graph. During `preview` the value is literally unknown (the bucket doesn't exist yet), so the promise resolves to an unknown sentinel or never settles, and the resulting `Promise<string>` gets exported as a raw promise — Pulumi serializes that as `{}` or throws on the engine RPC boundary.
2. **`pulumi.output("literal")`** — wrapping a plain string in an `Output` does nothing useful, defeats secret tracking, and makes the value show up in plaintext in the state file and in `pulumi preview --diff`. Secrets must come from `config.requireSecret()` so the encryption provider marks them.

The fix for #1 is `.apply()` (or `pulumi.interpolate`), for #2 is `requireSecret`.

## `index.ts`

```ts
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import * as aws from "@pulumi/aws";
import * as eks from "@pulumi/eks";

const config = new pulumi.Config();
const stack = pulumi.getStack();               // "dev" | "prod"
const isProd = stack === "prod";

const region = config.require("region");
const domainName = config.require("domainName");

// Secret never lives in Git in plaintext: `pulumi config set --secret dbPassword ...`
// stored encrypted-at-rest in Pulumi.<stack>.yaml under the stack's encryption provider.
const dbPassword = config.requireSecret("dbPassword");

const provider = new aws.Provider("aws", { region: region as aws.Region });
const opts = { provider };

// us-east-1 provider is mandatory for ACM certs consumed by CloudFront.
const usEast1 = new aws.Provider("aws-us-east-1", { region: "us-east-1" });

const tags = { Environment: stack, Project: "myapp", ManagedBy: "pulumi" };

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- S3 assets
const bucket = new aws.s3.BucketV2("app-bucket", {
    bucket: `myapp-assets-${stack}`,
    tags,
}, opts);

new aws.s3.BucketVersioningV2("app-bucket-versioning", {
    bucket: bucket.id,
    versioningConfiguration: { status: "Enabled" },
}, opts);

new aws.s3.BucketServerSideEncryptionConfigurationV2("app-bucket-sse", {
    bucket: bucket.id,
    rules: [{
        applyServerSideEncryptionByDefault: { sseAlgorithm: "AES256" },
        bucketKeyEnabled: true,
    }],
}, opts);

new aws.s3.BucketPublicAccessBlock("app-bucket-pab", {
    bucket: bucket.id,
    blockPublicAcls: true,
    blockPublicPolicy: true,
    ignorePublicAcls: true,
    restrictPublicBuckets: true,
}, opts);

// ------------------------------------------- prod-only cross-region replication
if (isProd) {
    const replicaProvider = new aws.Provider("aws-replica", { region: "us-west-2" });

    const replica = new aws.s3.BucketV2("app-bucket-replica", {
        bucket: `myapp-assets-${stack}-replica`,
        tags,
    }, { provider: replicaProvider });

    new aws.s3.BucketVersioningV2("app-bucket-replica-versioning", {
        bucket: replica.id,
        versioningConfiguration: { status: "Enabled" },
    }, { provider: replicaProvider });

    new aws.s3.BucketServerSideEncryptionConfigurationV2("app-bucket-replica-sse", {
        bucket: replica.id,
        rules: [{ applyServerSideEncryptionByDefault: { sseAlgorithm: "AES256" } }],
    }, { provider: replicaProvider });

    new aws.s3.BucketPublicAccessBlock("app-bucket-replica-pab", {
        bucket: replica.id,
        blockPublicAcls: true,
        blockPublicPolicy: true,
        ignorePublicAcls: true,
        restrictPublicBuckets: true,
    }, { provider: replicaProvider });

    const replicationRole = new aws.iam.Role("replication-role", {
        assumeRolePolicy: JSON.stringify({
            Version: "2012-10-17",
            Statement: [{
                Effect: "Allow",
                Principal: { Service: "s3.amazonaws.com" },
                Action: "sts:AssumeRole",
            }],
        }),
        tags,
    }, opts);

    // Correct Output composition: all() + apply, no await, no manual string concat
    // of unresolved values.
    new aws.iam.RolePolicy("replication-policy", {
        role: replicationRole.id,
        policy: pulumi.all([bucket.arn, replica.arn]).apply(([src, dst]) =>
            JSON.stringify({
                Version: "2012-10-17",
                Statement: [
                    {
                        Effect: "Allow",
                        Action: ["s3:GetReplicationConfiguration", "s3:ListBucket"],
                        Resource: [src],
                    },
                    {
                        Effect: "Allow",
                        Action: [
                            "s3:GetObjectVersionForReplication",
                            "s3:GetObjectVersionAcl",
                            "s3:GetObjectVersionTagging",
                        ],
                        Resource: [`${src}/*`],
                    },
                    {
                        Effect: "Allow",
                        Action: [
                            "s3:ReplicateObject",
                            "s3:ReplicateDelete",
                            "s3:ReplicateTags",
                        ],
                        Resource: [`${dst}/*`],
                    },
                ],
            })),
    }, opts);

    new aws.s3.BucketReplicationConfig("app-bucket-replication", {
        role: replicationRole.arn,
        bucket: bucket.id,
        rules: [{
            id: "assets-to-us-west-2",
            status: "Enabled",
            filter: {},
            deleteMarkerReplication: { status: "Enabled" },
            destination: { bucket: replica.arn, storageClass: "STANDARD" },
        }],
    }, opts);
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------ Networking
const vpc = new aws.ec2.Vpc("app-vpc", {
    cidrBlock: "10.0.0.0/16",
    enableDnsHostnames: true,
    enableDnsSupport: true,
    tags,
}, opts);

const azs = aws.getAvailabilityZonesOutput({ state: "available" }, opts);

const publicSubnets = [0, 1].map(i =>
    new aws.ec2.Subnet(`public-${i}`, {
        vpcId: vpc.id,
        cidrBlock: `10.0.${i}.0/24`,
        availabilityZone: azs.names[i],
        mapPublicIpOnLaunch: true,
        tags: { ...tags, "kubernetes.io/role/elb": "1" },
    }, opts));

const privateSubnets = [0, 1].map(i =>
    new aws.ec2.Subnet(`private-${i}`, {
        vpcId: vpc.id,
        cidrBlock: `10.0.${i + 10}.0/24`,
        availabilityZone: azs.names[i],
        tags: { ...tags, "kubernetes.io/role/internal-elb": "1" },
    }, opts));

const igw = new aws.ec2.InternetGateway("app-igw", { vpcId: vpc.id, tags }, opts);

const publicRt = new aws.ec2.RouteTable("public-rt", {
    vpcId: vpc.id,
    routes: [{ cidrBlock: "0.0.0.0/0", gatewayId: igw.id }],
    tags,
}, opts);

publicSubnets.forEach((s, i) =>
    new aws.ec2.RouteTableAssociation(`public-rta-${i}`, {
        subnetId: s.id,
        routeTableId: publicRt.id,
    }, opts));

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------- EKS
const cluster = new eks.Cluster("app-cluster", {
    name: `myapp-${stack}`,
    vpcId: vpc.id,
    publicSubnetIds: publicSubnets.map(s => s.id),
    privateSubnetIds: privateSubnets.map(s => s.id),
    nodeAssociatePublicIpAddress: false,
    skipDefaultNodeGroup: true,
    createOidcProvider: true,
    tags,
}, opts);

new eks.ManagedNodeGroup("app-nodes", {
    cluster,
    nodeGroupName: `myapp-${stack}-ng`,
    instanceTypes: [isProd ? "t3.large" : "t3.medium"],
    scalingConfig: {
        desiredSize: isProd ? 4 : 2,
        minSize: isProd ? 4 : 2,
        maxSize: isProd ? 8 : 3,
    },
    nodeRoleArn: cluster.instanceRoles.apply(rs => rs[0].arn),
    subnetIds: privateSubnets.map(s => s.id),
    tags,
}, opts);

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------- RDS
const dbSubnets = new aws.rds.SubnetGroup("app-db-subnets", {
    subnetIds: privateSubnets.map(s => s.id),
    tags,
}, opts);

const dbSg = new aws.ec2.SecurityGroup("app-db-sg", {
    vpcId: vpc.id,
    description: "Postgres access from cluster nodes only",
    ingress: [{
        protocol: "tcp",
        fromPort: 5432,
        toPort: 5432,
        securityGroups: [cluster.nodeSecurityGroupId],
    }],
    egress: [{ protocol: "-1", fromPort: 0, toPort: 0, cidrBlocks: ["0.0.0.0/0"] }],
    tags,
}, opts);

const db = new aws.rds.Instance("app-db", {
    identifier: `myapp-${stack}`,
    engine: "postgres",
    engineVersion: "16.1",
    instanceClass: isProd ? "db.t3.medium" : "db.t3.micro",
    allocatedStorage: isProd ? 100 : 20,
    dbName: "appdb",
    username: "appuser",
    password: dbPassword,                 // secret Output, encrypted in state
    dbSubnetGroupName: dbSubnets.name,
    vpcSecurityGroupIds: [dbSg.id],
    multiAz: isProd,
    storageEncrypted: true,
    publiclyAccessible: false,
    deletionProtection: true,
    backupRetentionPeriod: isProd ? 30 : 7,
    skipFinalSnapshot: false,
    finalSnapshotIdentifier: `myapp-${stack}-final`,
    tags,
}, opts);

// Connection string built with interpolate — stays a *secret* Output because
// dbPassword is secret; taint propagates automatically through interpolate.
const dbConnectionString = pulumi.interpolate
    `postgresql://appuser:${dbPassword}@${db.endpoint}/appdb?sslmode=require`;

new aws.secretsmanager.SecretVersion("app-db-conn", {
    secretId: new aws.secretsmanager.Secret("app-db-conn-secret", {
        name: `myapp/${stack}/db-connection`,
        tags,
    }, opts).id,
    secretString: dbConnectionString,
}, opts);

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------- IAM
// dev: programmatic-access IAM user. prod: OIDC-trusted role, no long-lived keys.
if (!isProd) {
    const user = new aws.iam.User("app-user", { name: `myapp-${stack}-sa`, tags }, opts);
    new aws.iam.AccessKey("app-user-key", { user: user.name }, opts);
    new aws.iam.UserPolicy("app-user-policy", {
        user: user.name,
        policy: bucket.arn.apply(arn => JSON.stringify({
            Version: "2012-10-17",
            Statement: [{
                Effect: "Allow",
                Action: ["s3:GetObject", "s3:PutObject", "s3:ListBucket"],
                Resource: [arn, `${arn}/*`],
            }],
        })),
    }, opts);
} else {
    const oidcArn = cluster.core.oidcProvider!.arn;
    const oidcUrl = cluster.core.oidcProvider!.url;

    const svcRole = new aws.iam.Role("app-svc-role", {
        name: `myapp-${stack}-irsa`,
        assumeRolePolicy: pulumi.all([oidcArn, oidcUrl]).apply(([arn, url]) =>
            JSON.stringify({
                Version: "2012-10-17",
                Statement: [{
                    Effect: "Allow",
                    Principal: { Federated: arn },
                    Action: "sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity",
                    Condition: {
                        StringEquals: {
                            [`${url}:sub`]: "system:serviceaccount:default:myapp",
                            [`${url}:aud`]: "sts.amazonaws.com",
                        },
                    },
                }],
            })),
        tags,
    }, opts);

    // Least privilege: explicit actions, explicit resources, zero wildcards.
    new aws.iam.RolePolicy("app-svc-policy", {
        role: svcRole.id,
        policy: bucket.arn.apply(arn => JSON.stringify({
            Version: "2012-10-17",
            Statement: [
                { Effect: "Allow", Action: ["s3:GetObject"], Resource: [`${arn}/*`] },
                { Effect: "Allow", Action: ["s3:ListBucket"], Resource: [arn] },
            ],
        })),
    }, opts);
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- HTTPS edge
const albSg = new aws.ec2.SecurityGroup("app-alb-sg", {
    vpcId: vpc.id,
    ingress: [{ protocol: "tcp", fromPort: 443, toPort: 443, cidrBlocks: ["0.0.0.0/0"] }],
    egress: [{ protocol: "-1", fromPort: 0, toPort: 0, cidrBlocks: ["0.0.0.0/0"] }],
    tags,
}, opts);

const alb = new aws.lb.LoadBalancer("app-alb", {
    loadBalancerType: "application",
    internal: !isProd,                       // dev = internal ALB
    subnets: (isProd ? publicSubnets : privateSubnets).map(s => s.id),
    securityGroups: [albSg.id],
    tags,
}, opts);

const tg = new aws.lb.TargetGroup("app-tg", {
    port: 8080,
    protocol: "HTTP",
    targetType: "ip",
    vpcId: vpc.id,
    healthCheck: { path: "/healthz", matcher: "200" },
    tags,
}, opts);

const albCert = new aws.acm.Certificate("app-alb-cert", {
    domainName: `${stack}.${domainName}`,
    validationMethod: "DNS",
    tags,
}, opts);

// 443 only. No forced 80 -> 443 redirect listener, per spec.
new aws.lb.Listener("app-https", {
    loadBalancerArn: alb.arn,
    port: 443,
    protocol: "HTTPS",
    sslPolicy: "ELBSecurityPolicy-TLS13-1-2-2021-06",
    certificateArn: albCert.arn,
    defaultActions: [{ type: "forward", targetGroupArn: tg.arn }],
}, opts);

let cdnDomain: pulumi.Output<string> | undefined;

if (isProd) {
    const cdnCert = new aws.acm.Certificate("app-cdn-cert", {
        domainName,
        validationMethod: "DNS",
        tags,
    }, { provider: usEast1 });

    const cdn = new aws.cloudfront.Distribution("app-cdn", {
        enabled: true,
        aliases: [domainName],
        origins: [{
            originId: "alb",
            domainName: alb.dnsName,
            customOriginConfig: {
                httpPort: 80,
                httpsPort: 443,
                originProtocolPolicy: "https-only",
                originSslProtocols: ["TLSv1.2"],
            },
        }],
        defaultCacheBehavior: {
            targetOriginId: "alb",
            viewerProtocolPolicy: "redirect-to-https",
            allowedMethods: ["GET", "HEAD", "OPTIONS"],
            cachedMethods: ["GET", "HEAD"],
            forwardedValues: {
                queryString: true,
                cookies: { forward: "none" },
            },
        },
        restrictions: { geoRestriction: { restrictionType: "none" } },
        viewerCertificate: {
            acmCertificateArn: cdnCert.arn,
            sslSupportMethod: "sni-only",
            minimumProtocolVersion: "TLSv1.2_2021",
        },
        tags,
    }, opts);

    cdnDomain = cdn.domainName;
}

// -------------------------------------------------------------------- Outputs
// All of these are Outputs, not Promises. The engine can render them as
// "(unknown)" during preview instead of blowing up on serialization.
export const bucketName = bucket.bucket;
export const bucketRegionalDomain = bucket.bucketRegionalDomainName;
export const bucketEndpoint = pulumi.interpolate`https://${bucket.bucketRegionalDomainName}`;
export const dbEndpoint = db.endpoint;
export const kubeconfig = pulumi.secret(cluster.kubeconfig);
export const albDnsName = alb.dnsName;
export const cdnDomainName = cdnDomain;
```

## `Pulumi.dev.yaml`

```yaml
config:
  aws:region: us-east-1
  myapp:region: us-east-1
  myapp:domainName: example.com
  myapp:dbPassword:
    secure: AAABAJ0h... # pulumi config set --secret dbPassword <value>
```

## `Pulumi.prod.yaml`

```yaml
config:
  aws:region: us-east-1
  myapp:region: us-east-1
  myapp:domainName: example.com
  myapp:dbPassword:
    secure: AAABAF9k...
```

## What changed and why

| Original | Fixed | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| `await arn` inside `async function` | `pulumi.interpolate` / `.apply()` | Keeps the value inside the Output graph; renders as unknown during preview instead of crashing |
| `export const bucketEndpoint = <Promise>` | exports an `Output<string>` | The engine cannot serialize a bare Promise into the stack outputs |
| `pulumi.output("plain-text-password")` | `config.requireSecret("dbPassword")` | Marks the value secret so it's encrypted in state and redacted in diffs |
| `deletionProtection: false` | `true` | AC #2 |
| `skipFinalSnapshot: true` | `false` + snapshot id | Prevents silent data loss on destroy |
| no `backupRetentionPeriod` | 7 (dev) / 30 (prod) | AC #2 |
| no `storageEncrypted` / `publiclyAccessible` | `true` / `false` | AC #2 |
| `versioning` only | + SSE + PublicAccessBlock | AC #1 |
| hardcoded `db.t3.medium` | `isProd` ternary | AC #5 / env sizing |
| `config.get("env")` | `pulumi.getStack()` | Stack name *is* the environment; avoids drift between stack and config |

## The general rule

Never `await` an `Output`. During `pulumi preview` the underlying resource does not exist, so its properties are unknown — `apply` callbacks are simply skipped and the result stays unknown, which is exactly the behavior you want. `await` bypasses that machinery and also silently drops the dependency edge, so Pulumi can reorder resource creation and produce nondeterministic failures even when preview happens to survive.

Use `pulumi.interpolate` for string building, `.apply()` for single-value transforms, and `pulumi.all([...]).apply()` for multi-value ones. Reserve `pulumi.output()` for lifting a `Promise<T>` or plain `T` that you genuinely need to feed into an Output-typed input — never for a literal you already control.
